Input: {"question": "Who is the artist of the album \"Double Live\"?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d00", "start": 0, "end": 156, "text": "Double Live (Butthole Surfers album) Double Live is a live double album by American punk band Butthole Surfers, released on vinyl and cassette tape in 1989."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d00", "start": 157, "end": 197, "text": "An expanded CD edition followed in 1990."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d00", "start": 198, "end": 594, "text": "All songs were written by Butthole Surfers, except: \"The One I Love,\" written by Bill Berry, Peter Buck, Mike Mills, and Michael Stipe of R.E.M.; \"Paranoid,\" written by Mark Farner of Grand Funk Railroad; \"No Rule,\" written by Jonas Almqvist of Leather Nun; and \"Kuntz,\" a distorted version of \"The Fear (กลัวดวง)\" ( written by Kong Katkamngae and performed by Phloen Phromdade, two Thai artists."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d00", "start": 595, "end": 603, "text": "This was"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d01", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "Double Live (Rheostatics album) Double Live is a 1997 album by Rheostatics."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d01", "start": 76, "end": 245, "text": "It collects a variety of live performances by the band, ranging from intimate club settings to record store sessions to their arena tour with The Tragically Hip in 1996."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d01", "start": 246, "end": 344, "text": "The album includes a number of tracks which have never appeared on any previous Rheostatics album."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d01", "start": 345, "end": 419, "text": "In fact, one of these tracks, \"Good Canadian\", was improvised on the spot."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d01", "start": 420, "end": 545, "text": "The Hip's live album \"Live Between Us\", released the same year, documents a show for which Rheostatics were the opening band."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d01", "start": 546, "end": 612, "text": "Gordon Downie acknowledges and thanks Rheostatics at the beginning"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d02", "start": 0, "end": 188, "text": "1996 ) Double Live ( 1997 ) The Nightlines Sessions ( 1998 ) Professional ratings Review scores Source Rating AllMusic [ 1 ] The Province [ 2 ] Double Live is a 1997 album by Rheostatics ."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d02", "start": 189, "end": 360, "text": "It collects a variety of live performances by the band , ranging from intimate club settings to record store sessions to their arena tour with The Tragically Hip in 1996 ."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d02", "start": 361, "end": 466, "text": "[ 3 ] The album includes a number of tracks which have never appeared on any previous Rheostatics album ."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d02", "start": 467, "end": 525, "text": "One of these tracks , `` Good Canadian '' , was improvised"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d03", "start": 0, "end": 519, "text": "Double Live ( Rheostatics album ) - WikiMili , The Best Wikipedia Reader WikiMili Double Live ( Rheostatics album ) Last updated February 07 , 2021 1997 live album by Rheostatics Double Live Live album by Rheostatics Released 1997 Genre Indie rock Label DROG Records Producer Gary Stokes Rheostatics chronology The Blue Hysteria ( 1996 ) Double Live ( 1997 ) The Nightlines Sessions ( 1998 ) Professional ratings Review scores Source Rating AllMusic [ 1 ] The Province [ 2 ] Double Live is a 1997 album by Rheostatics ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d03", "start": 520, "end": 569, "text": "It collects a variety of live performances by the"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 0, "end": 11, "text": "GhostTunes."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 12, "end": 178, "text": "\"Double Live\" debuted at number 1 on the US \"Billboard\" 200, becoming Brooks' seventh, and number 1 on the Top Country Albums, Brooks' ninth number one Country album."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 179, "end": 250, "text": "In November 2006, \"Double Live\" was certified 21× Platinum by the RIAA."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 251, "end": 351, "text": "\"It's Your Song\" was re-recorded in the studio and released as a single, peaking at #9 in late 1998."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 352, "end": 451, "text": "Two of the album's other tracks charted on the \"Billboard\" charts in 1998 from unsolicited airplay."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 452, "end": 567, "text": "Double Live (Garth Brooks album) Double Live is the first live album by American country music artist Garth Brooks."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d04", "start": 568, "end": 595, "text": "It was released on November"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d05", "start": 0, "end": 54, "text": ": 25th Anniversary Edition , exclusive to GhostTunes ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0368-7360176c1546:d05", "start": 55, "end": 179, "text": "[ 7 ] Double Live was again re-released on November 20 , 2018 , as part of the Garth Brooks Anthology Part III : Live book ."}, "D6S3